-- Dodger — a lot of objects, moving fast, recycled rather than destroyed.
--
-- What this exercises:
--   * many instances of one class in motion at once (sprite budget pressure)
--   * recycling: an object that leaves the screen is put back at the top rather
--     than removed, which is what a real console does because allocation is not
--     a thing you do at 60 Hz
--   * `random` in a level rule, so the same six rocks make a different run every
--     time round — the one thing that turns "stand still and wait" into a game
--   * objects at staggered speeds, so the per-scanline count keeps changing
--   * a score, a target to reach, and a life count to lose it with

start play

-- One number decides every column every rock ever falls down. Change it and the
-- run is different; leave it and a replay is a replay, on every console.
seed 20260726

scene play

create object ship (width 1 cell, height 1 cell, speed 65vw, sprite hero.svg)
create object rock (width 1 cell, height 1 cell, sprite rock.svg)

create ship player in play (x centerx, y screenheight - 2)

create rock r1 in play (x 8vw, y 0, speed 22vh, direction south)
create rock r2 in play (x 24vw, y 4, speed 28vh, direction south)
create rock r3 in play (x 40vw, y 8, speed 25vh, direction south)
create rock r4 in play (x 56vw, y 2, speed 31vh, direction south)
create rock r5 in play (x 72vw, y 6, speed 26vh, direction south)
create rock r6 in play (x 88vw, y 10, speed 29vh, direction south)

-- A counter on its own is a number with no noun. The label is an ordinary `text`
-- object beside it, which costs nothing a number does not: both are drawn from
-- the same font, on the same layer, at cells the game chose.
create text dodgedtag in play (x 1, y 1, text "dodged:")
create number score in play (value 0, x 9, y 1)
create text livestag in play (x 1, y 2, text "lives:")
create number lives in play (value 3, x 8, y 2)

control player left (xdirection -1) on hold
control player right (xdirection 1) on hold

when player hits screenleft, screenright then xdirection as 0

-- Recycling, in one line for all six rocks. A level rule that names a class runs
-- once per instance with that instance bound as its subject, so `y` here means
-- "this rock's y". Written per-object this was six near-identical rules, and six
-- places to forget one.
--
-- The new column is drawn as it falls off the bottom, which is also the moment
-- it is scored. Six rocks on six fixed columns is a pattern you learn once and
-- then stand still in; six rocks on columns nobody wrote down is a game.
--
-- The draw is *around the ship*, not across the whole wall: `random` takes
-- expressions, so where the player is standing is an argument to it. A rock aimed
-- within five cells either way has to be stepped away from, which is the
-- difference between a hazard and weather. `clamp` keeps the column on the
-- playfield when the ship is against a wall.
--
-- Five *cells*, not five percent, and that is the whole reason this one is
-- absolute: the ship is one cell wide on every console, so a dodge window
-- measured in cells is the same window everywhere. Written as a share of the
-- width it would be nine columns on a Game Boy and seventeen on a Mega Drive —
-- the same game on paper and half as dangerous in the hand.
--
-- And because the draw happens at a *stated* moment — this rock, leaving the
-- screen — the sequence is the same in the preview, in the ROM and in every
-- replay.
when rock.y >= screenheight then (y, x, score.value) as (0, clamp(random(player.centerx - 5, player.centerx + 5), 0, screenwidth - 1), score.value + 1)

when player hits rock then (lives.value, rock.y, rock.x) as (lives.value - 1, 0, clamp(random(player.centerx - 5, player.centerx + 5), 0, screenwidth - 1))

when lives.value reaches 0 in play then scene as gameover
when score.value reaches 30 in play then scene as cleared

scene gameover

create text over in gameover (x centerx - 4, y centery, text "game over")

when a pressed in gameover then scene as play

scene cleared

create text clear in cleared (x centerx - 6, y centery, text "all dodged")

when a pressed in cleared then scene as play
